# Winter's Embrace — Calendar and Character List

**Version:** 0.5.0
**Source:** Winter's Embrace (Fantasy Flight Games), the calendar and the character list
**Publisher:** Fantasy Flight Games

---

> **Day 1**
>
> The PCs have been invited to a formal tea ceremony with the renowned and legendary Crane courtier Kakita Ryoku and her apprentice Lady Chiyoe (see page 8 for the start of this day and page 25 for Ryoku’s profile). During this day, the PCs participate in the ceremony and learn that Ryoku has a task for them: discover how and why the Mantis were invited to this year’s Winter Court.

> **Day 8**
>
> The PCs are invited to a luncheon with Kakita Ryoku and her old friend and ex-lover Otomo Sorai (page 20). If the PCs haven’t discovered the Mantis plot to install Lady Magami as the new Empress and ascend to Great Clan status, Ryoku fills them in with her own spin. Ryoku implores the PCs to make embarrass the Mantis by setting Lady Magami up for failure in the upcoming play The Tale of the Fisherman’s Daughter.

> **Days 3-4**
>
> For these next two days, the PCs have the opportunity to prepare for the upcoming poetry competition and pursue their own personal goals at the Court (page 14). Each PC will have the opportunity to perform a total of three downtime activities each day. If they wish to engage in a narrative scene during this time, the scene may take the place of one of their downtime activities for all of the PCs involved.

> **Days 10-11**
>
> The PCs have a few days before the play to decide what they wish to do: interact with NPCs, forge alliances, and make their preparations (page 21). They may also pursue their own personal goals at Court, with a total of three downtime activities each day. If they wish to engage in a narrative scene during this time, the scene may take the place of one of their downtime activities for all of the PCs involved.

> **Day 6**
>
> PCs have another day to pursue their own interests and advance in their goals (page 17). Each PC has the opportunity to perform a total of three downtime activities during day 6. If they wish to engage in a narrative scene during this time, the scene may take the place of one of their downtime activities for all of the PCs involved. Note that Susano-o no Izen may attempt to imply the NPCs to help him further the Mantis’ cause if the PCs develop a relationship with him.

> **Day 13**
>
> The PCs are challenged to a duel, depending on whether they helped Lady Magami or sabotaged her (page 22). The outcome of the duel will have the court talking for weeks, and could have a dramatic impact on the PC’s reputation.

> **Day 2**
>
> After their meeting with Ryoku, one or more of the PCs find that they have been challenged to a Game of Letters by an anonymous sender (page 11). The GM chooses which NPC sent the letter, and what event they might appear at. There are two events, the Cliffside Archery Demonstration (page 12) and the Snow Lantern Celebration. The PCs meet several prominent NPCs on this day. They also learn of the upcoming poetry competition.

> **Day 9**
>
> Whether the PCs are working for Susano-o no Izen or Ryoku, they must make a choice whether to interfere with the upcoming performance of The Tale of the Fisherman’s Daughter (page 20). They meet Doji Shigeru and have the chance to discover his other persona, Lady Shike.

> **Day 5**
>
> The day of the poetry competition and Lady Magami’s debut (page 14). PCs have an opportunity to help Asahina Takako with preparations beforehand, and could earn a boon from the spirit of the lake. PCs may discover who their anonymous letter writer is this day, and have the opportunity to participate in the competition. Afterwards, some or all of the PCs may be invited to an exclusive after party where they can get to know some of the NPCs better and further their goals.

> **Day 12**
>
> It is the day of the play and the Emperor is in attendance (page 21). The PCs now have the opportunity to watch their plans come to fruition. Perhaps they sabotaged Lady Magami, or instead aided her. It’s possible they chose to do nothing. In any case, the play unfolds and one group or another will come out on top.

> **Day 7**
>
> On day 7 PCs receive a foreboding warning from an unknown source that tells them to stop their lines of inquiry regarding the Mantis invitation (page 18). This may provoke the PCs to search for the actual invitation. This day details ways they might find the invitation, as well as an encounter with the shinobi who seeks to keep the truth hidden. A chase ensues, and PCs must decide whether to side with the shinobi or honor their word to Ryoku.

> **Day 14**
>
> This is the last day of the adventure proper, and the PCs are given the chance to explore once again a relationship or rivalry they’ve developed over the course of the last fourteen days (page 23). Depending on what choices they made throughout, the PCs may have gained great honor for advancing the interests of their clan, but they may have also made powerful enemies and allies along the way.

## ACT I: Storms Roll Ashore

## ACT II: The Tale of the Fisherman’s Daughter

PERMISSION GRANTED TO PRINT ALL PAGES OF THIS BOOK FOR PERSONAL USE ONLY.

Asahina Takako (Crane): Daughter of the Asahina family daimyō, up-and-coming artificer, and priest overseeing the ceremonies of the poetry competition. Takako is gentle and kind, and hopes that the conflicts of the court can be resolved without bloodshed. She uses the Scholarly Shugenja profile found on page 314 of the core rulebook. More information on Takako can be found on page 30.

Doji Chiyoe (Crane): Second cousin to Doji Hotaru, Chiyoe has been groomed as a candidate for betrothal to the crown prince since she was young. Though she is well-educated and serves as Kakita Ryoku's apprentice, she is ignorant of the hardships of the peasantry. Chiyoe is poised and lovely, and is also devoutly religious. She uses the Seasoned Courtier profile found on page 313 of the core rulebook with the Spiritualist template. More information on Chiyoe can be found on page 30.

Doji Hatsuhina (Crane): Deputy seneschal of Kyūden Doji, Hatsuhina is a talented courtier and one of the primary hosts during this Winter Court. Once betrothed to Otomo Koryusai, she was cast aside when a more politically advantageous match took her place. Angry and bitter, Hatsuhina now seeks to take revenge on Koryusai by flaunting a catch of her own. Her profile can be found on page 24.

Doji Shigeru/Lady Shike (Crane): Crane clan director and performer, Doji Shigeru moonlights as the famous and mysterious Lady Shike. Presently, Lady Shike is slated for the role of Doji Mioko in The Tale of the Fisherman's Daughter. They use the Seasoned Courtier profile found on page 313 of the core rulebook with the Artist template. More information on Shigeru can be found on page 30.

Ikoma Rumiko (Lion): Famed Kabuki actor and playful by nature, Rumiko has been cast as the island spirit in The Tale of the Fisherman's Daughter. She is secretly a Lion clan shinobi and the one who forged the Mantis' invitation. Her profile can be found on page 26.

Kakita Ryoku (Crane): Legendary courtier and writer of the famed novel Winter, Ryoku is an active player in Rokugani politics and is heavily invested in disgracing the Mantis in order for the Crane to back out of their trade agreement with them. Her profile can be found on page 25.

Lady Magami (Mantis): Niece of Lord Yoritomo, the Mantis Clan Champion, Magami is educated and has trained all her life to be a candidate for betrothal to the crown prince. She makes her debut at the poetry competiton, but her true purpose of making an impression on the Emperor is secret. She uses the Seasoned Courtier profile found on page 313 of the core rulebook with the Sage template. More information on Magami can be found on page 30.

Miya Satoshi (Imperial): Imperial Herald with a hidden agenda, Satoshi is the daimyō of the Miya family. His goal at this year's Winter Court is to sow as much chaos as possible, as part of his endeavor to follow the tenants of the Kolat. His profile can be found on page 27.

Otomo Koryusai (Imperial): An overworked and under-resourced young man in the Imperial bureaucracy, Koryusai spends much of his time trying to fix all of the problems that his superiors, like Imperial Herald Miya Satoshi, blame him for. Koryusai would happily bear this burden if only he were able to win back the affections of Doji Hatsuhina, to whom he was once betrothed. His profile can be found on page 28.

Susano-o no Izen (Mantis): Trusted captain in the Mantis' Storm Fleet, Izen embodies much of what the Crane and the rest of the Empire finds distasteful about the Mantis. He is loud, gleeful, and speaks his mind. At the Winter Court, he acts as Lady Magami's retainer and seeks to ensure her safety and success––but plans to have a bit of fun doing it. His profile can be found on page 29.

Lord Yoritomo (Mantis): Mantis Clan Champion and leader of the Storm Fleet, Yoritomo seeks to raise the status of the Mantis Clan from merely a Minor Clan to that of a Great Clan. He is charming and fearless, and wishes only to bring greatness and honor to his Clan. He is Lady's Magami's uncle, and has spent years helping her prepare for her debut as a candidate for betrothal to the crown prince. He uses the Venerable Provincial Daimyō profile found on page 315 of the core rulebook with the Warrior template. More information on Yoritomo can be found on page 31.

